From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Vishnefske <jvishnefske@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 14:52:41 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] std: a backend for *-unknown-linux-none on linux_none_rt

std/build.rs sets cfg(linux_none) for linux with an empty target_env,
and std depends on linux_none_rt there. Each sys subsystem gets a
linux_none arm ahead of the unix one:

- pal/linux_none: init (stdio fds, SIGPIPE, args), cvt, the futex API
  and Timespec (unix/time.rs with clock_gettime from rt)
- alloc, env, io/error (a thread-local errno), is_terminal, random,
  paths, exit, pipe: small arms or cfg branches in the unix files
- fd, fs (statx, getdents64), thread (rt::thread, hermit-style TLS
  destructors), process (unix/common.rs plus rt::process spawning and
  pidfd), net (socket/mod.rs over a netc shim with libc's signatures)
- thread_local: the destructor list, run by each thread on exit
- kernel_copy: none yet; io::copy goes through a buffer
- os::fd and os::unix::net use rt and the netc shim; os::unix::thread's
  JoinHandleExt is not implemented (there are no pthreads)

library/Cargo.toml patches libc to ../libc (musl's types for
linux-none) and makes linux_none_rt a workspace member.
